  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "JJ had an array AAA of length NNN such that 0≤Ai&lt;2300 \\le A_i \\lt 2^{30}0≤Ai​&lt;230 for all 1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N.\n\nHe listed down the XOR of all the subsequences of AAA of size ≥(N−1)\\ge (N - 1)≥(N−1) in some **random** order. Let's call the XOR of these (N+1)(N + 1)(N+1) subsequences as B1,B2,…,BN+1B_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_{N+1}B1​,B2​,…,BN+1​.\n\nUnfortunately, he lost the initial array AAA. Can you help him recover it?\n\nIf there are multiple arrays which satisfy the given conditions, print any. Also, it is guaranteed that corresponding to the given input, an answer always exists.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line will contain TTT - the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN - the size of the initial array AAA.\nThe second line of each test case contains (N+1)(N + 1)(N+1) integers B1,B2,…,BN+1B_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_{N+1}B1​,B2​,…,BN+1​ - the XOR of all the subsequences of AAA of size ≥(N−1)\\ge (N - 1)≥(N−1) in some **random** order.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output NNN integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ which satisfy the given conditions.\n\n\nIf multiple answers exist, print any.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤Bi&lt;2300 \\leq B_i \\lt 2^{30}0≤Bi​&lt;230",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105.",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (40 points):**",
      "NNN is **odd**",
      "**Subtask 2 (60 points):**",
      "Original constraints."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
