        "input": "2\n3\n2 3 0 1\n5\n27 15 23 30 29 31",
        "output": "1 2 3\n1 2 4 8 16",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nLet ⊕\\oplus⊕ denote the bitwise XOR operation.\n\n\nTest Case 1: A=[1,2,3]A = [1, 2, 3]A=[1,2,3] satisfies all the conditions since [2,3,0,1]=[1⊕3,1⊕2,1⊕2⊕3,2⊕3][2, 3, 0, 1] = [1 \\oplus 3, 1 \\oplus 2, 1 \\oplus 2 \\oplus 3, 2 \\oplus 3][2,3,0,1]=[1⊕3,1⊕2,1⊕2⊕3,2⊕3]\n\n\nTest Case 2: A=[1,2,4,8,16]A = [1, 2, 4, 8, 16]A=[1,2,4,8,16] satisfies all the conditions since [27,15,23,30,29,31]=[1⊕2⊕8⊕16,1⊕2⊕4⊕8,1⊕2⊕4⊕16,2⊕4⊕8⊕16,1⊕4⊕8⊕16,1⊕2⊕4⊕8⊕16][27, 15, 23, 30, 29, 31] = \n[1 \\oplus 2 \\oplus 8 \\oplus 16, 1 \\oplus 2 \\oplus 4 \\oplus 8, 1 \\oplus 2 \\oplus 4 \\oplus 16, 2 \\oplus 4 \\oplus 8 \\oplus 16, 1 \\oplus 4 \\oplus 8 \\oplus 16, 1 \\oplus 2 \\oplus 4 \\oplus 8 \\oplus 16][27,15,23,30,29,31]=[1⊕2⊕8⊕16,1⊕2⊕4⊕8,1⊕2⊕4⊕16,2⊕4⊕8⊕16,1⊕4⊕8⊕16,1⊕2⊕4⊕8⊕16]"
      },
